/* Minimal pairs, and the sentences that tell them apart.

   Tested with the app's own voice on the device she uses. The article is
   always spoken, because that is how German is heard — nobody parses a bare
   noun in speech, and the article is often what carries the distinction.

   tier 1  the article decides it: der Bruder against die Brüder
   tier 2  same article, so the word itself decides
   tier 3  barely audible; the sentence is offered as a hint
   tier 4  not audible at all; context is the only route, and the game says
           so rather than telling her to listen harder

   ok:true on a sentence means it contains a word she has already met
   besides the target. Tiers 3 and 4 draw only from those, because a clue
   she cannot read is not a clue. */

